{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/535165-vtr-1e-setting-liberty-city-by-night","id":535165,"title":"(VTR 1e Setting) Liberty City By Night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-31T21:07:56-07:00","id":535165,"title":"(VTR 1e Setting) Liberty City By Night","content":"<i>Welcome to Liberty City, where the only dirty word is hope....</i><br /> <br /> Alright, the following setting thread is for a crossover of old-school Requiem and Grand Theft Auto, specifically the games of the 3D Era (GTA III, Vice City, San Andreas, Liberty City Stories, and Vice City Stories), and while it may seem a little ridiculous, this is a dream setting for me. As for the material, we are currently only using the materials found in the 1e WoD corebook and the 1e Requiem corebook, but as the setting expands, I will draw material from other 1e Requiem books and maybe do material for Changeling: The Lost and Hunter: The Vigil as well.<br /> <br /> Some things to take note of in my Requiem games....<ul><li>The Strix and God-Machine do NOT exist in this setting at all. Period. As a consequence, Demon: The Descent has been written out of this setting and Clan Julii was just Clan Ventrue under another name.</li> <li>Humanity and Predator's Taint have also been similarly excised, as well as the whole 1e &quot;Vampires are emotionally dead&quot; garbage.</li> <li>Since this is 1e, we will be using Virtues and Vices, not Masks and Dirges.</li> <li>Vampires of high blood potency can still feed on humans and animals, even after they hit BP 7 or higher.</li> <li>This iteration of the New World of Darkness is very un-gothic. Personal Horror is no longer the focus of the setting, instead it focuses on political intrigue and drama, mixed with dark action-adventure influenced by shonen anime.</li> <li>I may include material from fan games later on.</li> </ul><br /> Now, onto the base of the setting.....<br /> <br /> <br /> For centuries, Liberty City has been ruled by Caesar, an Invictus Daeva elder who has resided in the region since the time of the first European colonists. Caesar has always been a fair ruler, allowing the other four covenants to set up residence in Liberty City so long as they paid a tax to the Invictus. However, on January of 2015, Caesar had met Final Death at the hands of an unknown assailant, and now the city is in a state of chaos for the Kindred. Without a Prince, several Kindred are vying for the position of the leader of the city, and now Liberty City is ripe for any covenant to take over in full. Can the Invictus retain their power? Will a different covenant take over the city? Or will the whole power structure of Liberty City's Kindred collapse completely?<br /> <br /> Several noted vampires in the city include....<br /> <br /> <b>Salvatore Leone, </b>an ultra-paranoid Ventrue elder with strong underworld and mafia ties and de facto leader of the Invictus. in the wake of Caesar's death. He essentially wishes to maintain the status quo that Caesar had established.<br /> <b>Leon Hart, </b>a Gangrel ancilla of the Bruja Bloodline and leader of the Carthians in Liberty City, hoping to overthrow Invictus rule and give a fair chance to the downtrodden neonates in the city. The Carthians in Liberty City are modeled after a biker gang.<br /> <b>Samuel McCourt, </b>a very powerful Mekhet elder and tyrannical Bishop of Liberty City's Sanctified, wishing to take full control of Liberty City by subjugating the Invictus and exterminating the Circle of the Crone, Carthians, and Ordo Dracul.<br /> <b>Relena, </b>a Daeva elder and Hierophant of the local Acolytes. Much like Salvatore Leone, she wants to maintain Caesar's old policies, only with the other covenants paying tribute to the Circle of the Crone instead of the Invictus.<br /> <b>Papa Nero, </b>a Nosferatu elder and de facto leader of the Ordo Dracul. He has declared that the Ordo Dracul will stay out of this conflict, but does he have ulterior motives?<br /> <br /> <br /> More Kindred will be detailed and the aforementioned ones will be expanded upon as I work on the setting further.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T00:26:14-07:00","id":535340,"title":"","content":"I don't get the point of the thread. Is it to discuss the setting? Is it an Actual Play setting where we'll be reading the adventures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T05:46:59-07:00","id":535480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/535165-vtr-1e-setting-liberty-city-by-night?p=535340#post535340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the point of the thread. Is it to discuss the setting? Is it an Actual Play setting where we'll be reading the adventures?</div> </div> </div> </div>A little bit of both, it's a setting developmental thread where I can bounce ideas off for a chronicle and then from there, we'll read the adventures once I post them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T08:58:20-07:00","id":535655,"title":"","content":"Alright.. in that case, it all depends on where the characters come in this? How powerful they are planned to be? Neonates? Ancilae? Street level shmugs, some mid tier guys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:15:38-07:00","id":535740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/535165-vtr-1e-setting-liberty-city-by-night?p=535655#post535655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright.. in that case, it all depends on where the characters come in this? How powerful they are planned to be? Neonates? Ancilae? Street level shmugs, some mid tier guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neonates probably, most likely street level or mid-tier at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T23:36:05-07:00","id":536613,"title":"","content":"So who's the NPCs they're gonna be fighting? who's gonna be their lvl opponents? Since you don't get to throw around elders that easily. Unless you're just a pawn of another elder, and as I understand that's not really the game you're looking for","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T06:36:06-07:00","id":536937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/535165-vtr-1e-setting-liberty-city-by-night?p=536613#post536613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So who's the NPCs they're gonna be fighting? who's gonna be their lvl opponents? Since you don't get to throw around elders that easily. Unless you're just a pawn of another elder, and as I understand that's not really the game you're looking for</div> </div> </div> </div>Still working on that, I am thinking Belial's Brood would make good starter opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:50:17-07:00","id":537408,"title":"","content":"You could take a page from <i>Saint's Row</i> or <i>The Warriors</i> and divide the city up between themed vampire gangs -- mini-covenants, basically. They don't have to be silly like SR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T16:19:43-07:00","id":537492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/535165-vtr-1e-setting-liberty-city-by-night?p=537408#post537408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could take a page from <i>Saint's Row</i> or <i>The Warriors</i> and divide the city up between themed vampire gangs -- mini-covenants, basically. They don't have to be silly like SR.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would actually be a great idea. I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:39:26-07:00","id":537536,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/98887-sandboxing-in-the-wod?p=100091#post100091\">That is how I've built my cities</a>, Saint's Row is a great inspiration for it. Players seem to like it. Please let us know how the game goes.<br /> <br /> For vampire, the first game I ran the first antagonists were werewolves and lesser vampires. One of the characters got into a romantic thing with the werewolves, who were Pure I had taken from the Rockies book. There was this interesting dynamic between the alpha, Red Snow, who was this ultramasculine violence fantasy incarnate like something out of Robert Howard, and the omega, Black Sky, who's this pretty boy who idolizes Red Snow. So that was fun. In our more recent game the players started off as ghouls, mostly, and their original antagonists were hunters, some of whom were abusing their power, and a single vampire of the Lancea et Sanctum with ghoul minions who was making a power play with the help of another vampire, a traitor to the Circle of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-02-2015, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:20:00-07:00","id":538578,"title":"","content":"I know you're trying to limit yourself to the cores, but <b>Damnation City</b> really is the first and last word on city building in World of Darkness. If you're trying to run a game about the political machinations of different gangs with their own distinct territories, it's hard to beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:07:33-07:00","id":538775,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Damnation City is just really, really good. It's not a supplement your players need to read if you use it, either. It's just more advice for you to use in constructing your city, creating places with distinct identities, and some other miscellaneous tidbits of advice that will be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}